{"step_index":32,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-20T01:51:07Z","content":"You're right — I gave you my own analysis instead of running the full skill protocol. Let me do it properly now.\n\n**Running `/youtube-thumbnail-pro` — Full Protocol**\n\n---\n\n**Context loaded from image analysis:**\n- **Video Title:** Atomic Habits Explained in Hindi | James Clear\n- **Topic:** Hindi audiobook/book summary of Atomic Habits\n- **Niche:** Self-help book summaries (Hindi, faceless channel)\n- **Audience:** Hindi-speaking Indians, 18–35, mobile-first\n- **Content Type:** Educational / Audiobook Summary\n- **Channel:** Faceless — NO host face, emotion must come from scene + color\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Title-Thumbnail Pairing\n\n**Chosen Pattern: `Topic + Promise`**\n\n| Element | Content |\n|---|---|\n| **Thumbnail text** | Names the subject — `ATOMIC HABITS` |\n| **Title** | Creates the value gap — `Atomic Habits Explained in Hindi \\| James Clear \\| Full Audiobook` |\n| **Anti-redundancy check** | ✅ Thumbnail = WHAT. Title = HOW/WHY. They don't repeat. |\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Design Thinking (Internal Process)\n\n**Step 1 — Curiosity Gap:**\nShow the book as a physical object with POWER around it — but don't show *what* the habits are. The question: *\"What's inside this book that changed everything?\"* Show the result-energy, not the process.\n\n**Step 2 — Four C's Check:**\n\n| C | Assessment |\n|---|---|\n| **Clarity** | ONE focal point: the book. Text is secondary, not competing |\n| **Contrast** | Dark bg (#080C1A) vs white book vs yellow text = maximum pop |\n| **Consistency** | Matches SoulArc DNA: real cover, dark bg, bold text |\n| **Character** | Faceless — emotion comes through color temperature + lighting on the book |\n\n**Step 3 — Skeptic / Expert / Scroller:**\n- *Skeptic:* \"Why click this over 10 other Atomic Habits videos?\" → Answer: The thumbnail needs ONE differentiator — either scale of text, color, or supporting visual that others don't use\n- *Expert:* Current v2 has the staircase still, book doesn't have framing, \"JAMES CLEAR\" too large\n- *Scroller:* On a phone at 120px — only the two biggest words survive. Must be \"ATOMIC\" + \"HABITS\" in two colors. Everything else is noise.\n\n**Step 4 — Technical:**\n- 16:9, 1920×1080\n- Bottom-right CLEAR\n- Text: 3 words max visible at mobile size\n- Book cover fills 35% of frame\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3 → Phase 4: Output — 3 Concepts\n\n---\n\n### Concept 1: The Power Object\n**The go-to SoulArc-match. Safest. Highest replication accuracy.**\n\n**Pairing Pattern:** Topic + Promise\n**Style:** Minimal / Data-Evidence\n**Curiosity Gap:** The book glows with restrained power — what's inside it that creates such energy?\n**Emotion:** Rank 2 — **Curiosity** (#2 most effective for CTR)\n**Composition:** Rule of Thirds — book at left intersection, text owns right two-thirds\n\n**Visual Description:**\nReal Atomic Habits book cover (cream, tilted 12° left, floating 8px above a dark reflective floor with a soft shadow beneath). Background is near-black navy `#080C1A`, completely clean except a single ultra-faint atomic orbit circle (two ellipses crossing) centered behind the book at 8% opacity — barely visible, like a watermark. The book has a hairline warm-gold rim light on its left spine edge only — subtle, not glowing.\n\n**Color Palette:**\n- Primary: Deep Navy `#080C1A` — tension, premium, focus\n- Secondary: Pure Yellow `#FFD700` — urgency, attention (ATOMIC)\n- Accent: Pure White `#FFFFFF` — clarity (HABITS)\n\n**Text Overlay:**\n```\nLine 1: \"ATOMIC\"    → #FFD700 yellow, Impact/Anton weight, massive, flat, 3px black outline\nLine 2: \"HABITS\"    → #FFFFFF white, same size as ATOMIC, same flat style, 3px black outline  \nLine 3: \"JAMES CLEAR\" → #999999 grey, 28% the height of above lines\n```\nPositioned: right-aligned, vertically centered in right 65% of frame. Bottom-right CLEAR.\n\n**Safe Zone:** ✅ Bottom-right clear\n\n**Why This Works:** Two-color split on the title words (`ATOMIC` yellow / `HABITS` white) creates instant visual hierarchy. At 120px phone size, only these two words survive — which is exactly what you want. The near-empty background makes it look human-designed, not AI.\n\n**IMAGE GENERATION PROMPT:**\n```\n16:9 YouTube thumbnail, 1920x1080, professional flat graphic design style (NOT cinematic CGI, NOT Midjourney fantasy).\n\nLEFT 35%: Real published \"Atomic Habits\" book by James Clear — cream/white cover with atomic dot pattern and Penguin logo. Book tilted 15° clockwise, floating above a dark reflective floor, soft drop shadow beneath. Very thin warm gold rim light on left spine edge only. Thin dark vignette border around the white cover so it doesn't bleed into background.\n\nBACKGROUND: Deep near-black navy #080C1A, completely clean. ONE subtle element only: two faint ellipses (atomic orbit shape) behind the book, 8% opacity, same dark blue — barely visible like a watermark. NO stairs. NO arrows. NO icons. NO glow effects.\n\nRIGHT 65% TEXT (flat, bold, stacked):\n- \"ATOMIC\" — massive Impact-weight sans-serif, flat #FFD700 yellow, 3px black outline, NO metallic, NO bevel, NO gradient\n- \"HABITS\" — same massive size directly below, flat #FFFFFF white, 3px black outline\n- \"JAMES CLEAR\" — 28% the size of above, #999999 light grey, same flat style\n\nAll text right-aligned, vertically centered. Bottom-right corner empty.\n\nStyle rule: looks like a human made it in Photoshop. Flat color fills. No AI over-rendering. High contrast. Readable at 120px.\n```\n\n---\n\n### Concept 2: The Transformation Split\n**Higher CTR ceiling. More emotionally charged. Best for Hindi self-improvement audience.**\n\n**Pairing Pattern:** Emotion + Specificity\n**Style:** Before / After (implied, not literal)\n**Curiosity Gap:** Left side dark (old life) vs right side has the book + yellow energy (new life). The question: \"What changed?\"\n**Emotion:** Rank 3 — **Joy / Excitement** (aspiration, not fear)\n**Composition:** Split Frame — dark left half, energized right half\n\n**Visual Description:**\nFrame is split vertically. Left 20%: deep black `#000000`, fading to the dark navy center. Right 80%: the book + text layout on dark navy. The split creates an implied before/after without a person. Book centered-left in the right zone, text stacked on far right. A single thin bright gold vertical line separates the halves — 2px, the only decoration.\n\n**Color Palette:**\n- Primary: Black → Navy gradient `#000000` → `#080C1A`\n- Secondary: Gold accent `#FFD700`\n- Accent: White `#FFFFFF`\n\n**Text Overlay:**\n```\n\"ATOMIC\"    → #FFD700 yellow, massive flat bold\n\"HABITS\"    → #FFFFFF white, massive flat bold\n\"James Clear\" → small, #AAAAAA grey\n```\n\n**Safe Zone:** ✅ Bottom-right clear\n\n**Why This Works:** The implied split (dark → light) gives the Hindi self-improvement viewer a subconscious before/after hit without needing a face. The gold dividing line is the only accent element — one rule, one break.\n\n**IMAGE GENERATION PROMPT:**\n```\n16:9 YouTube thumbnail, 1920x1080, flat Photoshop design style.\n\nBACKGROUND: Deep dark navy #080C1A. Left 15% fades to pure black #000000. A single 2px vertical gold line at the 18% mark separates the dark left strip from the main composition. Nothing else decorating the background.\n\nCENTER-LEFT (book zone, 30-55% of frame width): Real published \"Atomic Habits\" book cover by James Clear. Angled 12° clockwise, floating, soft drop shadow. Thin dark border around white cover.\n\nRIGHT 45% (text zone):\n- \"ATOMIC\" — massive flat #FFD700 yellow, Impact weight, 3px black stroke, NO texture\n- \"HABITS\" — same size, flat #FFFFFF white, 3px black stroke\n- \"James Clear\" — small, #AAAAAA grey, same flat bold style\n\nAll text right-aligned. Vertically centered. Clean bottom-right.\n\nDo NOT add: stairs, arrows, glow, icons, sparkles, people, hands, coins.\n```\n\n---\n\n### Concept 3: The Floating Atom (Pattern Interrupt — Stand Out in Feed)\n**Highest pattern interrupt. Different from every other book thumbnail. Risk: less familiar = needs strong title to compensate.**\n\n**Pairing Pattern:** Question + Teaser\n**Style:** Mystery / Reveal\n**Curiosity Gap:** The book floats inside an atomic structure — the message: \"this book is a force of nature, not just a book\"\n**Emotion:** Rank 5 — **Mind-blown** (big revelation energy)\n**Composition:** Center Dominant — book dead center, atomic rings around it, text flanking\n\n**Visual Description:**\nBook centered in the frame (not left-third — this concept breaks the formula intentionally). Around the book: three thin white atomic orbital rings at different angles, very minimal line weight, 40% opacity. Background pure dark `#050A14`. Text split — \"ATOMIC\" top-left of book, \"HABITS\" bottom-right of book, framing the book like a title card. This is a PATTERN INTERRUPT concept.\n\n**Color Palette:**\n- Primary: Ultra-dark `#050A14`\n- Secondary: Electric yellow `#FFE000`\n- Accent: Cold white `#F0F0FF`\n\n**Text Overlay:**\n```\n\"ATOMIC\"    → top-left of book, #FFE000 yellow, massive flat bold\n\"HABITS\"    → bottom-right of book, #F0F0FF white, massive flat bold\n\"JAMES CLEAR\" → very small, below book center, #888888\n```\n\n**Safe Zone:** ✅ Bottom-right clear\n\n**Why This Works:** Every Hindi audiobook thumbnail puts the book on the left and text on the right. This one puts the book in the center and wraps the text around it — forces a scroll-stop because it looks different.\n\n**IMAGE GENERATION PROMPT:**\n```\n16:9 YouTube thumbnail, 1920x1080, minimal flat design.\n\nBACKGROUND: Ultra-dark near-black navy #050A14, clean.\n\nCENTER (book): Real \"Atomic Habits\" book cover by James Clear, centered in frame, tilted 5° only (almost straight), floating, very soft shadow. Thin 3 orbital rings around the book — simple white ellipses, 1.5px line weight, 35% opacity, three different angles creating an atomic symbol effect around the book.\n\nTEXT:\n- \"ATOMIC\" — large flat #FFE000 electric yellow, Impact weight, 2px black stroke — positioned top-left of book, above-left\n- \"HABITS\" — same size, flat #F0F0FF white — positioned bottom-right of book, below-right\n- \"JAMES CLEAR\" — tiny, #888888, centered below book\n\nStyle: Minimal. Clean. No glow on the rings — just thin lines. No metallic. No icons. No stairs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## A/B Test Suggestion\n\n**Test Concept 1 vs Concept 2**\n- Hypothesis: Does the split-frame implication of before/after (`Concept 2`) outperform the clean power-object layout (`Concept 1`) for Hindi self-improvement audience?\n- Metric: CTR after 48 hours minimum / 500 impressions\n- Prediction: Concept 1 wins on mobile (cleaner), Concept 2 wins on desktop (more visual drama)\n\n---\n\n**Bottom line on vidIQ's output:** The v2 thumbnail it generated is `Concept 1` — but half-executed. The staircase is still there, \"JAMES CLEAR\" is too large, and the book has no framing border. **Concept 1's prompt above** fixes all three. Paste it into vidIQ Thumbnail Generator as the `userQuery` and it should nail it on the next pass.","thinking":"The user wants me to use the youtube-thumbnail-pro skill properly. I already read the SKILL.md earlier. Let me now apply it fully to the SoulArc Studios Atomic Habits thumbnail situation.\n\nLet me run through the full skill protocol:\n\n**What I have:**\n- Video Title: \"Atomic Habits Explained in Hindi | Life-Changing Habit Building Lessons\"\n- Video Topic: Hindi audiobook/book summary of Atomic Habits by James Clear\n- Channel Niche: Self-help & psychology book summaries in Hindi (faceless channel)\n- Target Audience: Hindi-speaking Indians, 18-35, interested in self-improvement\n- Content Type: Summary/Audiobook (Educational/Tutorial-ish)\n\nI'm now working through the pairing pattern (topic + promise), the design thinking phases including curiosity gap, the Four C's, skeptic/expert/scroller review, and technical validation, before moving into concept building with emotion ranking, color psychology, and composition — aiming to produce 3-5 full thumbnail concepts.\n\nSince the channel is faceless (Hindi audiobook niche, dark backgrounds, metallic bold text, real book covers), emotion has to come through scene and color rather than a host's face. I'm now ready to build three strong concepts around that constraint."}
